                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Keeping your trucks on the road and out of the shop is essential to running a profitable operation. But even experienced fleet managers and owner-operators can overlook key maintenance practices that quietly eat into profits.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A single preventable breakdown can cost thousands of dollars in repairs, not to mention the downtime and lost revenue while a truck sits idle.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we've seen it all, from worn-out brake systems to neglected oil changes, and we know how much difference the right maintenance plan can make. Here are the most common semi truck maintenance mistakes that cost fleets big money, and how to avoid them.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
