                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-1-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "It's easy to push back a scheduled service when trucks are busy. But neglecting preventive maintenance is one of the fastest ways to shorten a vehicle's lifespan. Simple checks like oil changes, coolant levels, and air filter replacements are designed to catch small problems before they become expensive ones.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistake-1-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "According to the American Transportation Research Institute, maintenance and repair costs account for roughly 9% of total fleet expenses, and much of that stems from preventable issues. Staying consistent with your maintenance schedule keeps your engines running smoothly, improves fuel efficiency, and reduces breakdown risk on the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
